    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0311" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v06/pg289"/>

                <head>104. Message From President Kennedy to Chairman Khrushchev<anchor n="0" xml:id="d104-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-05-29">May 29,
                    1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Chairman</hi>: I am happy to inform you that
                    the date of July 28, 1963, which you suggest for the arrival of Secretary
                        Rusk in Moscow, is satisfactory. I
                    have asked Secretary Rusk to get in touch
                    with Minister Gromyko well in advance of
                    this date in order to work out the arrangements, including a public announcement
                    at an appropriate agreed time.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d104-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
